    "result": "Perfect! The bug has been successfully fixed. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## The Bug\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file because the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the frai-gate CLI. This happened because Commander parses flags separately from positional arguments, so the `args` array only contained `['init']` and missed the `--ci` flag.\n\n## The Fix\nI modified the `gate` command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 742-753) to:\n1. Accept the Command object as a second parameter\n2. Extract all arguments directly from `process.argv` after the 'gate' subcommand instead of relying on Commander's parsed args\n3. Pass all those arguments (including flags) through to the frai-gate CLI\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was tested and confirmed working:\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 The workflow file contains the correct CI configuration\n- \u2705 The rebuild with `pnpm --filter frai build` completed successfully",
